# The posture checks known to fail on every form of a kind (make check;
# test/boot, test/cage):
#
#   dev ID...    on any form built with DEV=1, as make check builds them
#   * ID...      on any form built as it ships
#   ARCH ID...   on that architecture (x86_64, aarch64)
#
# A form takes the dev or * line, the ARCH line, and the weaknesses its
# own form.yaml names, each with its excuse (forms/README.md). ?ID may
# fail or not, as the host decides. Each is a weakness still open
# (docs/security.md, "Not yet"): test/boot fails a machine on any other
# failure, and on any of these that starts passing, so no list can claim
# less, or more, than the machines hold.
#
# No form carries a shell but those that log people in (sshd, lima,
# prod-ssh) and DEV=1 builds, which add busybox-full: its shell, awk,
# wget, nc and telnetd. make check-dist boots prod-ssh's release disk as it
# ships: busybox for the logins sshd serves, and sshd listening.
#
# The boot chain is not verified end to end yet (docs/design/
# verified-boot.md): Secure Boot is off (?boot-secure-boot: it is on
# wherever the firmware takes the key), Alpine's kernel does not enforce
# module signatures (boot-sig-enforced), and no TPM counter guards the
# slot serial (boot-rollback-protected). Phase 4 and phase 5 close these.

dev network-no-login programs-no-downloaders programs-no-interpreters programs-no-shell ?boot-secure-boot boot-rollback-protected boot-sig-enforced
* ?boot-secure-boot boot-rollback-protected boot-sig-enforced
